        },
        "content": {
          "kind": "html",
          "value": "<div style='position:relative;width:1870px;height:2030px;background:#ffffff;color:#0f172a;overflow:hidden'><div style='position:absolute;left:40px;top:30px;width:1790px;border-top:3px solid #0f172a'></div><div style='position:absolute;left:40px;top:42px;font:800 12px/16px system-ui;letter-spacing:.18em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#6d28d9'>Twilite Zone · Library</div><div style='position:absolute;left:40px;top:70px;width:1790px;border-top:1px solid #0f172a'></div><div style='position:absolute;left:40px;top:96px;width:1790px;font:500 72px/74px Newsreader,Iowan Old Style,Palatino Linotype,Book Antiqua,Georgia,serif;letter-spacing:-.025em'>Primitives</div><div style='position:absolute;left:40px;top:188px;width:900px;font:italic 400 22px/30px Newsreader,Iowan Old Style,Palatino Linotype,Book Antiqua,Georgia,serif;color:#475569'>The fifteen parts every graph is made of, in the order a reader, an author and a builder meet them. Each has a page that says what it means, what it must do, and where it lives.</div><div style='position:absolute;left:40px;top:290px;width:1790px;border-top:3px solid #6d28d9'></div><div style='position:absolute;left:40px;top:312px;font:800 12px/16px system-ui;letter-spacing:.18em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#6d28d9'>Reading</div><div style='position:absolute;left:40px;top:338px;width:170px;font:400 14px/20px system-ui;color:#475569'>What a reader meets: graphs, their nodes and edges, and the Portals between them.</div><div style='position:absolute;left:40px;top:580px;width:1790px;border-top:1px solid #0f172a'></div><div style='position:absolute;left:40px;top:602px;font:800 12px/16px system-ui;letter-spacing:.18em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#0f172a'>Making</div><div style='position:absolute;left:40px;top:628px;width:170px;font:400 14px/20px system-ui;color:#475569'>What an author makes a graph from, and how it looks.</div><div style='position:absolute;left:40px;top:870px;width:1790px;border-top:1px solid #0f172a'></div><div style='position:absolute;left:40px;top:892px;font:800 12px/16px system-ui;letter-spacing:.18em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#0f172a'>Building</div><div style='position:absolute;left:40px;top:918px;width:170px;font:400 14px/20px system-ui;color:#475569'>How a graph is put together, connected to others, and made to act.</div><div style='position:absolute;left:40px;top:1740px;width:1790px;border-top:1px solid #0f172a'></div><div style='position:absolute;left:40px;top:1762px;font:800 12px/16px system-ui;letter-spacing:.18em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#0f172a'>Retiring</div><div style='position:absolute;left:40px;top:1788px;width:170px;font:400 14px/20px system-ui;color:#475569'>Leaving in favour of Methods. Kept until the behaviour build replaces them.</div></div>"
        }
      },
      "positionLocked": true
    },
